It drives the refusal through the `FA_FLUTTER_FAIL` wiring (the stub fails every invocation, so the smoke command itself dies rather than failing a pin check) and asserts the same never-tagged / never-published invariants as the `staleBumpLockfile` case: exit 1, `refusing to tag/publish v0.1.496`, no tag on the bump sha, no `gh release create` in the gh log. The `lockfileFails` parameter and its `FA_FLUTTER_FAIL` wiring are no longer dead — the path they model (a transient/broken toolchain during the smoke) is now covered.
